---
import "@fontsource-variable/geist/wght.css";
import "@fontsource-variable/geist-mono/wght.css";
import "katex/dist/katex.min.css";
import "../styles/app.css";
import "chessground/assets/chessground.base.css";
import "chessground/assets/chessground.brown.css";
import "chessground/assets/chessground.cburnett.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>∇ Nabla</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Nabla is a chess engine that chooses moves by energy descent on ray-transport fields."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="top">
      <h1><span class="sym">∇</span> Nabla</h1>
      <p class="lede">Nabla is a chess engine that chooses moves by energy descent on ray-transport fields.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="desk">
      <aside class="judge" aria-label="Judge">
        <p class="judge-kicker">Judge</p>
        <div class="judge-picks" role="group" aria-label="Who scores the position">
          <button type="button" data-judge="nabla" aria-pressed="true">Nabla</button>
          <button type="button" data-judge="stockfish" aria-pressed="false">Stockfish</button>
          <button type="button" data-judge="maia" aria-pressed="false">Maia</button>
        </div>
        <p class="pole">Black</p>
        <div class="meter" id="meter" style="--share: 0.5"><i id="meter-fill"></i></div>
        <p class="pole">White</p>
        <p id="judge-read">White grows up from the bottom of the bar.</p>
      </aside>

      <section class="board-column">
        <div class="board-well">
          <div id="rank-rail" class="rail ranks"></div>
          <div class="square-board">
            <div id="board"></div>
            <canvas id="fields"></canvas>
            <svg id="arrows" viewBox="0 0 8 8" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
            <div id="callout" class="callout" hidden></div>
            <div id="promo" hidden></div>
          </div>
          <div id="file-rail" class="rail files"></div>
        </div>
        <p id="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the engine.</p>
      </section>

      <aside class="panel">
        <fieldset class="seg">
          <legend>Match</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="you" checked /> You</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="mirror" /> Nabla vs Nabla</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="fish" /> Stockfish lite</label>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="knobs">
          <button id="new-game" type="button">New game</button>
          <button id="flip" type="button">Flip</button>
          <button id="pause" type="button">Pause</button>
          <label id="side-field"><span id="side-label">You play</span>
            <select id="side">
              <option value="white">White</option>
              <option value="black">Black</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label id="level-one">Nabla
            <select id="level">
              <option value="0">Level 0, the move</option>
              <option value="1">Level 1, captures</option>
              <option value="2" selected>Level 2, one reply</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <div id="level-pair" class="pair" hidden>
            <label>White
              <select id="level-w">
                <option value="0">Level 0</option>
                <option value="1">Level 1</option>
                <option value="2" selected>Level 2</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Black
              <select id="level-b">
                <option value="0">Level 0</option>
                <option value="1">Level 1</option>
                <option value="2" selected>Level 2</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <div id="fish-opts" class="pair" hidden>
            <label>Stockfish cap
              <select id="fish-elo">
                <option value="1320" selected>Elo cap 1320</option>
                <option value="1600">Elo cap 1600</option>
                <option value="2000">Elo cap 2000</option>
                <option value="full">No cap</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>Think
              <select id="fish-ms">
                <option value="200" selected>200 ms</option>
                <option value="500">500 ms</option>
                <option value="1000">1 s</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <label class="temp">Temperature <output id="temp-out">0.00</output>
            <input id="temp" type="range" min="0" max="500" value="0" step="5" />
          </label>
          <label class="temp">Pause before a move <output id="pace-out">500 ms</output>
            <input id="pace" type="range" min="0" max="1500" value="500" step="50" />
          </label>
        </div>

        <h2>Legend</h2>
        <figure class="legend-board">
          <svg id="legend-board" viewBox="0 0 6 6" role="img" aria-label="A small board. Hover a mark.">
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="6" height="6" fill="#b58863" />
            <g fill="#f0d9b5">
              <rect x="0" y="1" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="2" y="1" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="4" y="1" width="1" height="1" />
              <rect x="1" y="2" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="3" y="2" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="5" y="2" width="1" height="1" />
              <rect x="0" y="3" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="2" y="3" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="4" y="3" width="1" height="1" />
              <rect x="1" y="4" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="3" y="4" width="1" height="1" /><rect x="5" y="4" width="1" height="1" />
            </g>
            <g class="lm" tabindex="0" data-text="Blue at the rim. White controls that square more than Black. The centre stays clear so a piece can sit on it.">
              <rect class="hit" x="1" y="3" width="1" height="1" />
              <rect class="wash blue" x="1.08" y="3.08" width="0.84" height="0.84" rx="0.12" />
            </g>
            <g class="lm" tabindex="0" data-text="Rust at the rim. Black controls that square more than White.">
              <rect class="hit" x="4" y="1" width="1" height="1" />
              <rect class="wash rust" x="4.08" y="1.08" width="0.84" height="0.84" rx="0.12" />
            </g>
            <g class="lm" tabindex="0" data-text="Corner ticks. Both sides bear on the square. Turn the layer on with Tension.">
              <rect class="hit" x="2" y="2" width="1" height="1" />
              <path class="ticks" d="M2.16 2.34 H2.34 V2.16 M2.84 2.16 V2.34 H2.66 M2.16 2.66 V2.84 H2.34 M2.66 2.84 H2.84 V2.66" />
            </g>
            <g class="lm" tabindex="0" data-text="The number is how many pawns the opponent wins by taking the piece. It sits in the corner, off the piece.">
              <rect class="hit" x="3" y="2" width="1" height="1" />
              <circle cx="3.78" cy="2.22" r="0.16" fill="#8d2f2a" />
              <text x="3.78" y="2.22" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#fffdf8" font-size="0.16">3</text>
            </g>
            <g class="lm" tabindex="0" data-text="Green arrow. The move about to be played. A paler arrow is another move that was considered. The chip is the move in chess notation.">
              <rect class="hit" x="1" y="4" width="1" height="2" />
              <polygon points="1.5,5.62 1.42,4.55 1.58,4.55" fill="#fffdf8" />
              <polygon points="1.5,5.55 1.44,4.62 1.56,4.62" fill="#1f6b45" />
              <polygon points="1.5,4.28 1.32,4.62 1.68,4.62" fill="#1f6b45" stroke="#fffdf8" stroke-width="0.03" />
            </g>
          </svg>
          <figcaption id="legend-caption">Hover a mark.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="layers">
          <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="control" checked /> Control</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="tension" /> Tension</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="threats" checked /> Hanging pieces</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" data-layer="moves" checked /> Candidate moves</label>
        </div>

        <h2>Energy now</h2>
        <p class="note">White-positive, in pawns. A gain for White grows to the right. This is the position, not the reason for the last move.</p>
        <div id="energy"></div>

        <h2>Why that move</h2>
        <p class="note">For a Nabla move, the score is the value of the move. The bars are how each term changed, from the side that moved.</p>
        <div id="reason"><p class="empty">No move to explain yet.</p></div>

        <h2>Moves it considered</h2>
        <ol id="candidates"></ol>

        <h2>Recorded results</h2>
        <p class="note">Self-play on one machine, 17 November 2026. These are not ratings against Stockfish or Maia. No such match is recorded yet.</p>
        <table class="results">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Comparison</th><th>Score</th><th>Conditions</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Level 1 vs Level 0</td>
              <td>+521 ± 120</td>
              <td>200 games, 189 wins, 8 losses, 3 draws. 4 s + 0.04 s. <code>noob_3moves.epd</code>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Level 2 vs Level 1</td>
              <td>+334 ± 76</td>
              <td>200 games, 170 wins, 21 losses, 9 draws. Same clock and book.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Time losses</td>
              <td>0</td>
              <td>1,000 games at each level, 2 s + 0.02 s, after the node budget.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Tuner</td>
              <td>0.1145 to 0.1134</td>
              <td>40 Level 0 games, 1,988 quiet positions. The fit was not installed.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </aside>
    </main>

    <article class="paper">
      <h2>The energy</h2>
      <p>Nine terms, white-positive, in pawn units. Equation (11) of the field model:</p>
      <p class="math" data-tex="E(S)=E_{\mathrm{mat}}+E_{\mathrm{flux}}+E_{\mathrm{terr}}+E_{\mathrm{ex}}+E_{\mathrm{king}}+E_{\mathrm{trop}}+E_{\mathrm{pawn}}+E_{\mathrm{conf}}+E_{\mathrm{tempo}}" data-display="true"></p>
      <p>The phase that tapers a coefficient from the middlegame to the endgame is equation (12):</p>
      <p class="math" data-tex="\varphi=\min\left(1,\frac{N_{N}+N_{B}+2N_{R}+4N_{Q}}{24}\right)" data-display="true"></p>
      <p>Colour antisymmetry is exact, equation (27):</p>
      <p class="math" data-tex="E(\mathcal{F}S)=-E(S)" data-display="true"></p>

      <h2>What the terms are</h2>
      <p>
        Each piece sends influence along the squares it can actually attack. A piece
        in the way weakens what gets through. A rook behind its own rook still
        presses hard (a battery). A rook behind an enemy piece continues past it,
        at a lower strength. Nabla plays the legal move that raises its own energy the most.
      </p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Material</dt><dd>Who has more wood. A pawn is 1.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Mobility</dt><dd>Safe squares a piece can use.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Territory</dt><dd>Who controls the board, with the centre counting more. Extra attackers on a square add less and less.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Exchange</dt><dd>Whether a capture wins material. A fork counts. One move cannot both grab and defend.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>King</dt><dd>Enemy influence on the king. A pawn shelter holds it down, and the danger cannot grow without limit.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tropism</dt><dd>A weak pull of pieces toward the enemy king, and king centralisation when little material is left.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Pawns</dt><dd>Passed pawns, isolated and doubled pawns, and whether the enemy king can catch a passer.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Confinement</dt><dd>In an ending, how small a region the losing king can still reach.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tempo</dt><dd>A tenth of a pawn for having the move.</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <h2>How far it looks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Level 0</strong> scores the position after each move, and the forced replies when that move gives check.</li>
        <li><strong>Level 1</strong> also plays out captures.</li>
        <li><strong>Level 2</strong> also looks at every reply, then plays out captures. This is the default.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is a little lookahead, not zero and not a deep tree. On one desktop, a
        middlegame decision took about a millisecond at Level 0 and about twenty
        milliseconds at Level 2. Temperature 0 always plays the best of those moves.
        Raising it sometimes plays another move from the list.
      </p>
      <h2>Who can sit down</h2>
      <p>
        You can take White or Black, watch two Nabla levels play, or face Stockfish 19 lite.
        The Elo cap is Stockfish's own limit. The judge on the left is separate from the
        player: Nabla maps its energy, Stockfish lite reads the position at depth 8, and
        Maia is left to the gauntlet. The pause before a move is the wait after an arrow
        is drawn.
      </p>
      <p>
        The coefficients are still the hand-set values. <code>cargo run -p nabla-tune --release</code>
        prints a fit and does not install it. The same engine speaks UCI as <code>nabla</code>.
        To use the WebAssembly, copy <code>web/src/engine</code> after
        <code>npm run engine --prefix web</code>. Nabla is free software under the GNU GPL v3 or later.
        The Stockfish build in this page is GPL v3.
      </p>
    </article>
    <script>
      import { start } from "../scripts/play";
      start();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
